.Dd April 8, 2026
.Dt ZFSSUM-UPDATE 8
.Os
.
.Sh NAME
.Nm zfssum-update
.Nd update zfssum xattrs for every file in a ZFS dataset
.
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl a Ar algo
.Op Fl S
.Op Fl Z
.Op Fl v
.Op Fl -update
.Ar dataset
.Op Ar mountpoint
.
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
computes
.Xr zfssum 8
checksums for every regular file in
.Ar dataset
and stores the results as extended attributes on the mounted filesystem.
.Pp
Two xattrs are written per file:
.Bl -tag -width "user.zfssum.checksum"
.It Li user.zfssum.checksum
The hex-encoded digest.
.It Li user.zfssum.meta
A semicolon-separated string recording the algorithm, options, file
modification time
.Pq nanosecond precision ,
and file size at the time the checksum was computed.
Format:
.Li alg=blake3,size,holefill;mtime=1712345678.123456789;size=12345 .
.El
.Pp
The tool operates in two phases:
.Bl -enum
.It
.Sy "ZAP directory walk" :
the dataset's directory tree is traversed at the DMU level using
ZAP cursor APIs, building an in-memory mapping from object number to
relative path.
No VFS transitions occur during this phase.
.It
.Sy "Sequential object iteration" :
all objects in the dataset are visited in object-number order via
.Fn dmu_object_next .
For each regular file the block pointer checksum is computed and both
xattrs are written via
.Xr lsetxattr 2 .
Because dnode blocks hold approximately 32 adjacent dnodes,
sequential iteration maximizes ARC hit rates.
.El
.Pp
.Ar mountpoint
is required for xattr writes.
If omitted,
.Nm
reads
.Pa /proc/self/mounts
to find the ZFS mount for
.Ar dataset .
.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width "--skip-holes"
.It Fl a , -algo Ar algo
Hash algorithm used to combine block checksums.
Supported values:
.Cm blake3
.Pq default ,
.Cm sha256 ,
.Cm sha512 ,
.Cm bp .
See
.Xr zfssum 8
for details on each algorithm.
.It Fl S , -no-size
Do
.Em not
include the file size in the hash.
.It Fl Z , -skip-holes
Skip holes instead of filling zeros.
.It Fl v , -verbose
Print per-file hex digest and timing to standard error.
.It Fl -update
Before computing a checksum, read the file's existing
.Li user.zfssum.meta
from the SA xattr nvlist
.Pq at the DMU level, without a VFS call .
If the recorded algorithm, modification time, and file size all match the
current values, the file is skipped.
.Pp
Without
.Fl -update ,
checksums are computed for all files unconditionally and all xattrs are
overwritten.
.El
.
.Sh DIAGNOSTICS
Progress is printed to standard error once per second:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
[00:01:23] 12345/67890 files (18.2%) | 234.5 files/s | errors: 3
.Ed
.Pp
With
.Fl -update ,
a cached count is also shown.
On completion a summary line is printed:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
done: 67890 files, 12345 checksummed, 55545 cached, 0 errors in 1m23s
.Ed
.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Compute checksums for every file in
.Li tank/data :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# zfssum-update tank/data
.Ed
.Pp
Incremental update after a few files have changed:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# zfssum-update --update tank/data
.Ed
.Pp
Use SHA-256 and specify the mountpoint explicitly:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# zfssum-update -a sha256 tank/data /tank/data
.Ed
.
.Sh CAVEATS
The
.Fl -update
cache check reads the
.Li ZPL_DXATTR
SA attribute.
On datasets with
.Sy xattr Ns = Ns Cm dir ,
xattrs are not stored in SA and the cache check always reports a miss,
causing all files to be recomputed.
.Sy xattr Ns = Ns Cm sa
.Pq the default
is recommended.
.Pp
.Nm
opens the pool in read-only mode via
.Sy libzpool .
The pool must also be imported by the running kernel so that
.Xr lsetxattr 2
can write xattrs through VFS.
.Pp
Encrypted datasets are not supported because SA attributes are not
readable from userspace.
.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr lsetxattr 2 ,
.Xr zfssum 8 ,
.Xr zfs 8
